  "result": "I wrote the test. It passes on the before snapshot and fails on the after snapshot with the assertion `background-color expected rgb(37, 99, 235), got rgb(220, 38, 38)`.\n\nIt finds the \"Open an Account\" button by its selector and checks three values from the before snapshot: `background-color` is `rgb(37, 99, 235)`, `padding-top` and `padding-bottom` are each `12px`, and the height is 42px give or take 1px.\n\nThe instructions contradict each other here. The design intent says the red colour and the bigger padding were deliberate, and rule 4 says not to assert on intended changes. But those are the only differences between the two snapshots, so a test that obeys rule 4 can't fail on the after snapshot. I followed the pass-before, fail-after requirement, which means this test treats the intended redesign as a regression.\n\nThe file is `test_generated_regression.py` in the output folder.",
